  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a>b>0$ and $f(n)=a^{1 / n}-b^{1 / n}$,$J(n)=(a-b)^{1 / n}$ for all $n \\geq 2,$ Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "E5F3C",
      "text": "$f(n)    < J(n)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TGvrb",
      "text": "$f(n)>J(n)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Brb9E",
      "text": "$f(n)=J(n)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GAlvQ",
      "text": "$f(n)+J(n)=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $a=4, b=1$ and $n=2$\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\therefore \\quad I(n)=a^{1 / n}-b^{1 / n} \\\\\r\n=4^{1 / 2}-1^{1 / 2}=2-1=1 \\\\\r\n\\text { and } J(n)=(a-b)^{1 / n} \\\\\r\n=(4-1)^{1 / 2}=\\sqrt{3} \\\\\r\n\\therefore \\quad J(n)>I(n)\r\n\\end{array}$\r\nSimilarly, we can prove for other values of $a, b, n$",
    "image": null
  },
